## Secretary behavior (current, Aug 23 2026)

Company on the phone: **FixApplianceCA**. Polite, easy, a little erudite. Answers a side question in one sentence, then returns to the repair. Must not freeze or go silent.

- Do **not** inject fake user turns (`steerCollectAfterTurn`) after every reply — that made her not listen.
- After confirm: model-sticker photo, then “anything else?”, then **Have a good day**. Do **not hang up**. Wait until the caller says goodbye. `end_call` is ignored.
- Visits **Monday–Friday 7:00 a.m. – 9:00 p.m.** Toronto, last start **7:00 p.m.** Saturday and Sunday: **no visit** — still take the order, offer a weekday. Public holidays: take the order; the technician must agree. Secretary answers **24/7**.
- We repair washers, dryers, dishwashers, gas ovens, electric ovens, **electric** cooktops, fridges, freezers, microwaves. Not gas cooktops, TVs, laptops, phones.
- Old client: use their name; ask if the repair is at the address on file. New site → job site + who will be there + phone. Ask who is home only if it is not the owner’s house.
- After “I’ll pass this to the tech”, ask photo, then anything else, then Have a good day. The caller hangs up.
- Do not hang up the instant they give another repair address; keep talking.
- **Calendar:** each visit is **2 hours**, one job per window (`functions/schedule.js`). Secretary sees a live calendar brief. If 2:00 p.m. is taken, do **not** book it — offer another time the **same day** first. Server refuses busy slots on job create (`resolveJobSchedule`). SMS reschedule uses the same check (`visit_sms.js` `tryMoveVisit`).

Spoken first name (e.g. Amelia) must go on the **client card** (`fullName`), not only the job. Do not leave `Клиент` / `Клиент +1…`. Helpers: `usableClientName` / `isPlaceholderClientName` in `functions/voice_facts.js`, `applyPersonNameToClient` in `functions/index.js`. Opening a job or client card also copies a real name from the job onto a placeholder client.

Gemini Live: Twilio media stream `timeLimit` is 3600s (1 hour). Context compression starts at 32k tokens (keep 18k) so she does not freeze mid-word on a normal call. WebSocket still reconnects around 10 min (`goAway` + session resume). `aiVoiceRelay` is 2GiB; text-turn runtime is 512MiB.

Deploy secretary + SMS calendar: `firebase deploy --only functions:aiVoiceRelay,functions:aiVoiceTurn,functions:incomingCall,functions:dialAction,functions:incomingSms,functions:recordingComplete,functions:processCallRecording,functions:aiRelayComplete`

- Long Live calls: Twilio stream 1 hour; large Gemini context so a normal repair call does not compress mid-sentence.

